This product includes a MoonBit port of the Noise Protocol Framework handshake
state machine. The port follows the structure of snow:

  https://github.com/mcginty/snow
  Copyright Jake McGinty and contributors
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  or the MIT License, at your option.

Cryptographic primitives are provided by mooncry where noted in the README:

  https://github.com/cc06b/mooncry
  Copyright 2026 Solo Crypto Contributors
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

BLAKE2s-256, BLAKE2b-512, and the corresponding HMAC constructions are
implemented in this repository from RFC 7693 and RFC 2104. mooncry 0.95.0's
BLAKE2s and BLAKE2b are not used because they append an extra empty block when
the input length is a positive multiple of the block size.

Applicable Cacophony test vectors are vendored from snow's
tests/vectors/cacophony.txt. The original suite is
https://github.com/centromere/cacophony (Unlicense).

The TCP example is a separate module under example/tcp. It links
moonbitlang/async 0.22.9 and is not a dependency of the library.
That package is Copyright 2025 International Digital Economy Academy
and licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:
https://github.com/moonbitlang/async
The example does not copy its source. The published library archive
omits example/tcp.
